          "source_id": "foundation02-language-first10-collins-request",
          "status": "verified",
          "scope": "Verified selected ordinary-language consultation within root independent AI acceptance. Source finding: The selected countable noun is polite or formal asking for an action. Its displayed level is B1+. The selected POS is the noun, not the adjacent verbs. Literal selected source level: B1+. Other-sense labels not applied: {}. Independent decision: Accept the ordinary asking noun and optional polite/formal tendency. Editorial B1 is appropriate for the bounded support-message example; preserve literal Collins B1+ without asserting equivalence. Software requests and musical requests remain distinct. No human, subject-matter, morphology, media, domain, expression or release approval is claimed."
        }
      ],
      "editorial_notes": "Shared workplace foundation. The exact ordinary selected-sense definition, example and editorial difficulty have scoped independent AI language acceptance recorded by root. Accept the ordinary asking noun and optional polite/formal tendency. Editorial B1 is appropriate for the bounded support-message example; preserve literal Collins B1+ without asserting equivalence. Software requests and musical requests remain distinct. Retain the countable ordinary asking noun and make its common polite or formal tendency explicit without making courtesy a necessary condition. A sent request can be a message. Exclude the requesting verb, a software service-operation message, and formal specialist request instruments. Accepted forms, POS, region, morphology, image, word audio and historical reference prefix remain unchanged. Only the two newly added lexical references are verified for this bounded language decision. No whole expression, specialist procedure, authority, module or release approval is implied."
